# Generated by agents/build-standalone.mjs. Not tracked on purpose: it is a
# frozen copy of jarvis.html with the figures baked in, so committing it would
# put a second set of numbers in the repo that ages independently of the real
# ones. Rebuild it when you need it.
build/

# data/jarvis-data.json is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored: the Refresh
# JARVIS data workflow commits it so the published screen has real numbers.
#
# The rule that makes that safe: it may only ever contain figures already
# public in index.html. The Scout reads nothing else. If you later wire a
# private source — inbox contents, an unpublished deal, anything from the
# excluded job-search notes — that section belongs somewhere private, not in
# this file, because this repo is a public mirror.
